                                        "sense_id": "fa2af364-b8f1-3f4f-a07f-d08c9d638894",
                                        "entry_id": "858dfcb2-06f1-3cd7-89b0-005774a5f1f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To utter a slanderous statement about; baselessly speak ill of; to wrong."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d62d4a8-ce5f-4132-aa94-a077da5e9442",
                                                "sense_id": "fa2af364-b8f1-3f4f-a07f-d08c9d638894",
                                                "text": "Tuc[ca]. […] Can thy Author doe it impudently enough?\n Hiſt[rio]. O, I warrant you, Captaine: and ſpitefully inough too; he ha's one of the moſt ouerflowing villanous wits, in Rome. He will ſlander any man that breathes; If he diſguſt him.\n Tucca. I'le know the poor, egregious, nitty Raſcall; and he haue ſuch commendable Qualities, I'le cheriſh him: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
